ue)\r\n    related: Mapped[list[\"Related\"]] = relationship(secondary=\"link\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Related(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"related\"\r\n\r\n    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n\r\nlink_table = Table(\r\n    \"link\",\r\n    Base.metadata,\r\n    Column(\r\n        \"main_id\",\r\n        ForeignKey(\"main.id\", ondelete=\"CASCADE\"),\r\n        primary_key=True,\r\n    ),\r\n    Column(\r\n        \"related_id\",\r\n        ForeignKey(\"related.id\", onupdate=\"CASCADE\"),\r\n        primary_key=True,\r\n    ),\r\n    Column(\"is_deleted\", Boolean(), server_default=false(), default=False),\r\n)\r\n\r\nclause = Main.related.and_(\r\n    link_table.c.is_deleted.is_(other=False)\r\n)\r\n\r\nstmt = select(Main).join(clause)\r\nprint(stmt)\r\n```\r\nVersion 2.0.14 output:\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT main.id \r\nFROM main\r\nJOIN link AS link_1 ON main.id = link_1.main_id\r\nJOIN related ON \r\n    related.id = link_1.related_id \r\n    AND link.is_deleted IS false  -- link is aliased with `link_1`, so this throws an error\r\n```\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT main.id \r\nFROM main\r\nJOIN link AS link_1 ON main.id = link_1.main_id\r\nJOIN related ON\r\n    related.id = link_1.related_id\r\n    AND link_1.is_deleted IS false  -- Here a correct (aliased) table seems to be referenced\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\ncaused by 9f7c97b40b6b6c #9779","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11010/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]